  "name": "Screech Lead",
  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "Screech lead: FM Morph shifted +9 st (a one-shot Mod A pushes the Shift toward +12 on the attack), 3-voice unison, Saturate into a high-resonance note-tied Comb- and an LP12 at 6 kHz to keep the fizz in check. No sub. Play: F3-C5, an octave or two above the bass line, short phrases and held shrieks; mono legato with 50 ms portamento between overlapping notes. Tweak: Osc A Shift for the vowel of the shriek, Osc A Index for FM brightness, Filter A Res for ring, Filter B Freq for harshness. FX: Hard Clip +6 dB after a Pre high-pass at 300 Hz so only the shriek clips, multiband squash at 50 %, an EQ high shelf -2 dB at 9 kHz, Dimension (size 0.6) for width, a dotted-1/8 Ping-Pong delay (feedback 0.3, 300 Hz..6 kHz, 18 %) that answers each phrase, and a 2 s hall at 18 %. Harder hits push the FM and every note is detuned a little differently. Macros: Screech detunes and thickens the shriek, FM brightens the tone, Edge drives the clipper and Space adds the delay and hall.",
